For simple roots $\alpha_i$, the <Cartan matrix> is
$$
A_{ij}=\langle\alpha_i,\alpha_j^\vee\rangle
=\frac{2(\alpha_i,\alpha_j)}{(\alpha_j,\alpha_j)}.
$$
Its diagonal entries are two, while its off-diagonal entries encode the angles and relative lengths in the <Dynkin diagram>.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= ii
{parent=a}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=ii}

The <fundamental weight>[fundamental weights] $\omega_i$ are the basis dual to the simple coroots:
$$
\langle\omega_i,\alpha_j^\vee\rangle=\delta_{ij}.
$$

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= iii
{parent=a}
{scope}

= Solution
{parent=iii}

The <Dynkin label>[Dynkin labels] of a weight $\lambda$ are
$$
[\lambda^1,\ldots,\lambda^r],
\qquad
\lambda^i=\langle\lambda,\alpha_i^\vee\rangle,
$$
so $\lambda=\sum_i\lambda^i\omega_i$.

Solved by gpt-5.6-sol high.

= iv
{parent=a}
